nk":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T19:05:15-07:00","id":514707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starmage21</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/512869-do-you-like-your-bed?p=514456#post514456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like this:<br /> <a href=\"http://9gag.com/gag/aP4XWBK/bdsm-level-advanced\" target=\"_blank\">http://9gag.com/gag/aP4XWBK/bdsm-level-advanced</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That design irks me on multiple levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T20:36:49-07:00","id":514754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/512869-do-you-like-your-bed?p=514707#post514707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That design irks me on multiple levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please elaborate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T21:53:08-07:00","id":515825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/512869-do-you-like-your-bed?p=514754#post514754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please elaborate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The pillory/stock is made out of what looks like 2 pieces of 1x6 or 1x8, crude formed and lacking any padding. This is bad because being only 1&quot; thick it puts a lot of pressure on a relatively small cross section. The lack of padding, or at least rounding of hole, tends to make this even more of a pressure point problem. This is in addition to the fact that it makes it decidedly easier to shake and twist, which is trouble and can lead to unintentionally pinched flesh. Additionally, it's held on by a corner bracket and some cheap and simple wing nuts. They do not secure well against vibration (a critical factor) and the corner bracket means you've basically got a dangerously sharp edge on the end posts of the bed. Setting aside the danger presented by a bit of rough and tumble, you'd keep having problems with it stabbing/cutting against feet in the night when you sleep.<br /> <br /> Moving on to the frame construction, they have a total of 2 bolts per support holding the canopy support to the frame itself. That means that as the bolts start to slip with age there is nothing but those bolts preventing it from coming loose with vibration/time... which on something that presumably will see activity is less than ideal. The failure of the bed standing a good chance of crushing anyone in the cage is source of concern. There's also the fact that they didn't bother to paint the bolts over when they were done, but that's a minor gripe at best. <br /> <br /> The canopy is all one welded piece (I suspect it's a frame that got re-purposed) and while that means it's solid enough, it also likely means it would be used for attachment points... and there are not any. again relatively minor.<br /> <br /> The cage itself is primarily composed of what looks like standardized bar units, which is good and I have no particular problem with, except that the cage is either too large or the door to it is too small for emergencies. In the even of an emergency (such as someone passing out or a fire) you need to be able to open the cage and quickly extract them no matter where they are. The door is at most just enough for a small person to squeeze through, making reaching in to extract someone difficult at best.<br /> <br /> Final minor gripe is the size of the bed including canopy for the room. It's too tall to readily fit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Since I don't want to be purely negative...<br /> <br /> If I were to do something like this, I'd probably start with an open-top solid cage, get the gas-lift hardware from a storage bed and use it along with a frame and latch to secure the top. So a top-loading cage, easy to get someone out of if the need arises. This has the double advantage that some quick latching wood paneling around the outside would instantly turn it from &quot;bdsm cage&quot; to a a slightly unusually high storage bed. I would do the pillory as a separate unit, that rises on two steel legs made to double latch on each side to the corner support beams of the cage. Rubber layer glued to the connecting surfaces to negate minor vibration and avoid metallic rattling. That way it's solidly anchored enough and yet is fairly easy to remove as needed. padding on the anchor points, 2-3&quot; oak if I could manage it. I probably wouldn't bother with the canopy, but if I was going to do it, I'd probably have it be on it's own legs each with a double-lock over the corner legs of the main cage for security as needed (same set up as with the pillory). I would make the legs angle in slightly so that the canopy was actually a bit smaller than the bed, and make the legs themselves of the collapsible variety out of the same square steel tubing used for the cage. The reason for that is then the canopy can collapse it's legs and be small enough to store in the cage when not in use.<br /> <br /> End result? More flexibility, ability to be slightly subtle and ability to only have the features there when you want them, plus the ability to store everything away neatly under the bed when not in use, and overall less risk of problems.... IMO, YMMV, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T01:20:33-07:00","id":515926,"title":"","content":"Canuck is the Rotten Tomatoes/Wikipedia of bed knowledge. Noted. O_0","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T17:10:16-07:00","id":516567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/512869-do-you-like-your-bed?p=515926#post515926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canuck is the Rotten Tomatoes/Wikipedia of bed knowledge. Noted. O_0</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a fatass, I have had exactly 1 bed frame* that was purchased that lasted more than a year, and the ones I've built only clocked up to the 3 year mark. And I have a bit of a hang up on basic health and safety in relationship to BDSM practices. Never set up a restraint system that isn't capable of keeping a person 24 hours without medical issue or one that you can't get a person mobile enough to get out of the building in less than 180 seconds. <br /> <br /> I don't care what people do in their bed(or other)rooms as long as it's reasonably safe... the hospitals get busy enough without needing an emergency visit from someone that didn't know how to properly use a slipknot, how to check circulation or that thought that wet rawhide was a good wrist tie because they read about it in a porn.<br /> <br /> <br /> *-that one is going on 5 years now though, so I'm quite pleased with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T20:14:54-07:00","id":516672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/512869-do-you-like-your-bed?p=513164#post513164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got one of those memory foam ones. I'm always of two minds about it: on one hand, you find a comfortable position and you sink into it and you're good; on the other hand, you can find yourself sunk into the mattress in an UNcomfortable position and your sleeping body simply lacked the will to move. My back seems BETTER than it was on my old futon, but it's not great. It's not the lie we were sold.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have a memory foam one too. I really like it. Though, ours has a pillow top to it(weird right?), so you can't flip it or anything...<br /> <br /> But, for the most part, we really like it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/512869-do-you-like-your-bed?p=513246#post513246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My sister warns me against memory foam on the grounds that it collects too much heat. Since she is an actual reptile, a genuinely ecothermic being who cannot produce or maintain her own body heat, I take this complaint seriously. You memory foam advocates don't notice it getting too hot?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't notice it getting overly hot. My wife actually gets really cold...but, she's just naturally cold.<br /> <br /> Though....[see below]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/512869-do-you-like-your-bed?p=513256#post513256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The newer ones have cooling gel in the tops to help with this, but yes, expect to use a sheet more than a blanket. When it's <i>really </i>hot in the summer, I'll sleep on top of the sheet and comforter to avoid the heat absorption.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, in the summer I find I do that quite a bit(sleep on top of the covers). Hmmm....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:22:38-07:00","id":518506,"title":"","content":"I have a visco memory foam bed and its really comfortable. I knock out pretty quickly on it. My friends call my bed a &quot;whore&quot; cause it lures them all the time lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}